error[TY005]: cannot add Num and Str
 --> operand-types.lm:8:7
  |
8 | print(n + s)
  |       ^^^^^ mismatched operands
  |
  = note: `+` joins two Nums, two Strs or two Lists
  = note: to build a string from mixed values use interpolation: "${a}${b}"
  = note: or turn the other value into text first: `str(n)`

error[TY005]: cannot apply `*` to Num and Str
 --> operand-types.lm:9:7
  |
9 | print(n * s)
  |       ^^^^^ mismatched operands
  |
  = note: `*` wants two Nums
  = note: `"ab".repeat(3)` repeats a string

error[TY005]: cannot apply `**` to Num and Str
  --> operand-types.lm:10:7
   |
10 | print(n ** s)
   |       ^^^^^^ mismatched operands
   |
   = note: `**` wants two Nums

error[TY005]: cannot compare Num and Str
  --> operand-types.lm:11:7
   |
11 | print(n < s)
   |       ^^^^^ not comparable
   |
   = note: `<`, `<=`, `>` and `>=` work on two Nums or two Strs

error[TY005]: cannot add Bool and Bool
  --> operand-types.lm:12:7
   |
12 | print(b + b)
   |       ^^^^^ mismatched operands
   |
   = note: `+` joins two Nums, two Strs or two Lists

